IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pid-dates`
IMPORT `pid-disclosures`

-- Public Interest Disclosures Act 2022 (NSW) -- Part 3, Protections (ss 30-41), from the seat of the discloser, or of
-- anyone else who suffers detrimental action because of a disclosure or an investigation.
--
-- Questions: "Was what was done to me detrimental action?" (s 32), "Was it reasonable management action?" (s 31), "Is
-- the person who did it liable to me in damages?" (s 35), "Can their employer be ordered to pay?" (s 36), "Can I apply
-- for an injunction, and what can it order?" (s 37), "Can I be made to pay the other side's costs?" (s 38), "By what day
-- must a prosecution be started?" (s 33(6)), "Am I protected from liability for making the disclosure?" (ss 40, 7(2)),
-- "Can what I disclosed about my own past conduct be used against me?" (s 41).
--
-- Machinery and duties of agencies in Part 3 are out: s 34 (referral of evidence of an offence by agencies; nothing the
-- person can do or is owed). s 30 (the Part applies from the time the disclosure is first made) and s 39 (proceedings
-- under ss 35 and 37 need no prosecution, and survive an acquittal) are in comments: no fact under them changes an
-- answer.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; version as at 30 October 2023; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not
-- for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Public Interest Disclosures Act 2022 -- Part 3, Protections`

§§ `The nouns`

-- s 32(1) "detriment to a person means disadvantage to the person, including" (a)-(g); s 32(2) detrimental action is an
-- act or omission causing, comprising, involving or encouraging detriment or the threat of detriment.
DECLARE `What was done to me` IS ONE OF
    `injury, damage or loss caused to me`
    `damage to my property`
    `damage to my reputation`
    `intimidation, bullying or harassment`
    `unfavourable treatment in my career, profession, employment or trade`
    `discrimination, prejudice or adverse treatment`
    `disciplinary proceedings or disciplinary action`
    `some other disadvantage`
    `a threat of any of these, express or implied`
    `nothing that disadvantaged me`

-- s 32(3) "the following actions are not detrimental action".
DECLARE `What the action was` IS ONE OF
    `a lawful investigation of serious wrongdoing or other misconduct`
    `the lawful reporting or publication of a finding, or lawful adverse comment, resulting from such an investigation`
    `a prosecution for a criminal offence`
    `none of these`

-- s 31(3) "reasonable management action ... includes" (a)-(j).
DECLARE `What kind of action it was` IS ONE OF
    `it was not management action`
    `management action of a kind listed in section 31(3)`
    `some other management action`

-- s 40(1), ss 7(2)(b), 41(1): the liabilities the maker of a disclosure may worry about.
DECLARE `The liability I am worried about` IS ONE OF
    `civil liability, including for breaching a duty of secrecy or confidentiality`
    `criminal liability, including for breaching a confidentiality law or code of conduct`
    `disciplinary action`
    `liability for not complying with a duty to disclose information imposed by another law`
    `liability for my own past conduct that I revealed in making the disclosure`

-- s 37(2), (4): what an injunction may order.
DECLARE `The order I want` IS ONE OF
    `an order restraining conduct that would be a detrimental action offence`
    `an order requiring an act or thing to remedy a detrimental action offence`
    `a formal apology`
    `an order restraining an attempt to end my employment in a position or role`
    `reinstatement in the same or a substantially similar position or role`
    `some other order`

§§ `s 32 -- detrimental action`

@export Was what was done to me detrimental action under the NSW Public Interest Disclosures Act 2022 (s 32)?
GIVEN `what was done to me` IS A `What was done to me` @desc What the act or omission caused, comprised, involved or encouraged. One of: "injury, damage or loss caused to me", "damage to my property", "damage to my reputation", "intimidation, bullying or harassment", "unfavourable treatment in my career, profession, employment or trade", "discrimination, prejudice or adverse treatment", "disciplinary proceedings or disciplinary action", "some other disadvantage", "a threat of any of these, express or implied", "nothing that disadvantaged me"
      `what the action was` IS A `What the action was` @desc Whether the action was one the Act says is never detrimental action. One of: "a lawful investigation of serious wrongdoing or other misconduct", "the lawful reporting or publication of a finding, or lawful adverse comment, resulting from such an investigation", "a prosecution for a criminal offence", "none of these"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was it detrimental action` MEANS
    IF     `what the action was` EQUALS `none of these`
       AND (NOT (`what was done to me` EQUALS `nothing that disadvantaged me`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- s 32(3) "are not detrimental action"; s 32(1) "means disadvantage"

§§ `s 31 -- reasonable management action`

-- s 31(3) lists reasonable appraisal, counselling, suspension, decision to investigate, disciplinary action, transfer,
-- redundancy, contract review, promotion and benefit decisions, and related actions. s 31(4) "is not reasonable
-- management action if" (a) the way of taking it is not reasonable, (b) corruptly or fraudulently, (c) to conceal or
-- avoid the consequences of serious wrongdoing, or (d) the taker suspected, believed or was aware a public interest
-- disclosure had been or might be made, that was a contributing factor, and the action was not taken to reduce the
-- risk of detrimental action. Fork F4: action that is not management action at all, and listed action that is not
-- itself reasonable, are JUST FALSE; reasonable management action of a kind not listed is NOTHING (the list says
-- "includes").
@export Was the action taken against me reasonable management action, which the Act does not prevent (s 31)?
GIVEN `what kind of action it was` IS A `What kind of action it was` @desc One of: "it was not management action", "management action of a kind listed in section 31(3)" (appraisal of work performance, counselling, suspension from the workplace, a decision to investigate misconduct, disciplinary action, transfer or redeployment, redundancy or retrenchment, suspending, ending or reviewing a services contract, a decision about promotion, reclassification, transfer or a benefit, or a related action), "some other management action"
      `the action itself was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action itself was reasonable (a judgment for the court; answer on the view you want tested)
      `the way it was taken was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the way the action was taken was reasonable
      `it was taken corruptly or fraudulently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action was taken corruptly or fraudulently
      `it was taken to conceal serious wrongdoing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action was taken to conceal, or avoid the consequences of, serious wrongdoing
      `a suspected disclosure contributed to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person taking the action suspected, believed or knew (rightly or not) that a public interest disclosure had been, might have been, might be or was to be made, and that contributed to the action
      `it was taken to reduce the risk of detrimental action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action was taken to reduce the risk of detrimental action against you or someone else
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was it reasonable management action` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `what kind of action it was` EQUALS `it was not management action` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `the way it was taken was reasonable`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `it was taken corruptly or fraudulently` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `it was taken to conceal serious wrongdoing` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `a suspected disclosure contributed to it` AND (NOT `it was taken to reduce the risk of detrimental action`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `the action itself was reasonable`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `what kind of action it was` EQUALS `management action of a kind listed in section 31(3)` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 31(3) "includes": other management action is neither in nor out; fork F4)

§§ `s 33 -- the detrimental action offence`

-- s 33(1): a person must not take detrimental action against another if they suspect, believe or know that someone has
-- made (or may make) a public interest disclosure or is investigating serious wrongdoing, and that is a contributing
-- factor. Maximum penalty 200 penalty units or imprisonment for 5 years, or both; an indictable offence (s 33(3)); a
-- mistaken suspicion is no defence (s 33(2)); the accused bears the onus on the suspicion and the contributing factor
-- (s 33(4)); appropriate corrective action under s 66 is a defence (s 33(5)). The value of a penalty unit is set by the
-- Crimes (Sentencing Procedure) Act 1999, not deposited.
-- s 33(6) "Proceedings ... may be instituted at any time within 3 years after the offence is alleged to have been
-- committed." Fork F1: the last day is the same day three years on.
@export By what day must a prosecution be started against the person who took detrimental action against me (s 33(6))?
GIVEN `the day of the alleged offence` IS A DATE @desc The day the detrimental action offence is alleged to have been committed
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must a prosecution be started` MEANS `the day of the alleged offence` `plus months` 36

§§ `s 35 -- damages for detrimental action`

-- s 35(1) "A person who takes detrimental action against another person is liable in damages ... for injury, damage or
-- loss suffered as a result by the other person or a third person if" (a) the taker suspects, believes or is aware that
-- any person has made, may have made, may make or proposes to make a public interest disclosure, or is investigating
-- serious wrongdoing, and (b) that is a contributing factor. s 35(3): a mistaken suspicion does not matter. s 35(4): the
-- plaintiff establishes the detrimental action; the defendant must prove (a) no suspicion, belief or awareness, or (b)
-- that it was not a contributing factor -- so those are asked as "has the other side proved ...". s 35(5): appropriate
-- corrective action under s 66 is a defence. s 31(2)(a)(i): reasonable management action incurs no liability under
-- Part 3. s 35(7): no recovery for the same action under both s 35 and ICAC Act s 79J, Ombudsman Act s 31S or LECC Act
-- s 97I. s 35(6) exemplary damages may be included; s 35(8) compensation already received under s 62 is taken into
-- account; s 35(9) other remedies unaffected; s 35(10) the liability is not in tort; s 39 no prosecution or an
-- acquittal does not stop the claim. The Act sets no time limit for the claim (finding 4).
@export Is the person who took detrimental action liable to pay me damages under the NSW Public Interest Disclosures Act 2022 (ss 31, 32, 35)?
GIVEN `what was done to me` IS A `What was done to me` @desc What the act or omission caused, comprised, involved or encouraged. One of: "injury, damage or loss caused to me", "damage to my property", "damage to my reputation", "intimidation, bullying or harassment", "unfavourable treatment in my career, profession, employment or trade", "discrimination, prejudice or adverse treatment", "disciplinary proceedings or disciplinary action", "some other disadvantage", "a threat of any of these, express or implied", "nothing that disadvantaged me"
      `what the action was` IS A `What the action was` @desc One of: "a lawful investigation of serious wrongdoing or other misconduct", "the lawful reporting or publication of a finding, or lawful adverse comment, resulting from such an investigation", "a prosecution for a criminal offence", "none of these"
      `I can establish they took the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can establish that the person took that action (against you or against someone else)
      `I suffered injury, damage or loss as a result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered injury, damage or loss as a result of the action
      `they have proved they had no suspicion of a disclosure or investigation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person has proved that, when acting, they did not suspect, believe or know that anyone had made or might make a public interest disclosure, or was investigating serious wrongdoing
      `they have proved it was not a contributing factor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person has proved that any such suspicion, belief or knowledge was not a contributing factor to the action
      `what kind of action it was` IS A `What kind of action it was` @desc One of: "it was not management action", "management action of a kind listed in section 31(3)", "some other management action"
      `the action itself was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was management action: whether the action itself was reasonable
      `the way it was taken was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was management action: whether the way it was taken was reasonable
      `it was taken corruptly or fraudulently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action was taken corruptly or fraudulently
      `it was taken to conceal serious wrongdoing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action was taken to conceal, or avoid the consequences of, serious wrongdoing
      `it was taken to reduce the risk of detrimental action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action was taken to reduce the risk of detrimental action against you or someone else
      `it was appropriate corrective action under section 66` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action was appropriate corrective action taken by an agency under s 66 after a finding of serious wrongdoing or misconduct
      `I already recovered damages for it under another integrity Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already recovered damages for the same action under ICAC Act s 79J, Ombudsman Act s 31S or LECC Act s 97I
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the person liable to me in damages` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `I can establish they took the action`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT (`Was it detrimental action` `what was done to me` `what the action was` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `I suffered injury, damage or loss as a result`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `they have proved they had no suspicion of a disclosure or investigation` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `they have proved it was not a contributing factor` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `it was appropriate corrective action under section 66` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 35(5): this section gives no damages on these facts
           IF `I already recovered damages for it under another integrity Act` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 35(7) "not entitled"
           IF `management` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 31(2)(a)(i) "does not ... incur other liability under this Part"
           IF `management` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (whether it was reasonable management action is open; fork F4)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        -- The suspicion is not disproved here (the defendant has not proved its absence), so it counts for s 31(4)(d).
        `management` MEANS `Was it reasonable management action` `what kind of action it was` `the action itself was reasonable` `the way it was taken was reasonable` `it was taken corruptly or fraudulently` `it was taken to conceal serious wrongdoing` TRUE `it was taken to reduce the risk of detrimental action`

§§ `s 36 -- the employer's liability`

-- s 36 "A court may make the following additional orders if the court is satisfied damages are recoverable under section
-- 35 in circumstances where the person who took the detrimental action did so in connection with the person's position
-- or role as an employee": (a) the employer liable in whole or part, (b) joint or several liability.
@export Can the court order the employer of the person who took detrimental action to pay my damages (s 36)?
GIVEN `damages are recoverable from the person under section 35` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied you can recover damages from the person under s 35 (see the damages question)
      `they acted in connection with their position or role as an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person took the action in connection with their position or role as someone's employee
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the employer be ordered to pay` MEANS
    IF `damages are recoverable from the person under section 35` AND `they acted in connection with their position or role as an employee`
    THEN JUST TRUE  -- the court "may" order it
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 37 -- injunctions`

-- s 37(1) the Supreme Court may, on the application of (c) the maker of a public interest disclosure or (d) another
-- person against whom detrimental action has been or may be taken, grant an injunction "relating to the commission or
-- possible commission of a detrimental action offence". s 37(6) no injunction to restrain or remedy appropriate
-- corrective action under s 66 or reasonable management action. s 37(11) no application about the same matter under
-- both s 37 and ICAC Act s 79L, Ombudsman Act s 31U or LECC Act s 97K. s 37(7): a person taking management action bears
-- the onus of showing its reasons. s 37(8)-(9): an interim injunction may be granted, and no undertaking as to damages
-- may be required. Fork F5: an applicant outside (c)-(d), or conduct that is not even possibly a detrimental action
-- offence, is NOTHING (the grant is limited in its own words, without "only").
@export Can I apply to the NSW Supreme Court for an injunction against detrimental action (s 37)? No undertaking as to damages can be required for an interim injunction.
GIVEN `the kind of my disclosure` IS A `The kind of disclosure` @desc The kind of disclosure you made, if any (see "What kind of public interest disclosure did I make"). One of: "a voluntary public interest disclosure", "a voluntary public interest disclosure by determination of the head of an agency", "a witness public interest disclosure", "a mandatory public interest disclosure", "not a public interest disclosure"
      `detrimental action has been or may be taken against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether detrimental action has been, or may be, taken against you
      `the conduct is or would be a detrimental action offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct is, or would be, detrimental action taken because the person suspects, believes or knows of a disclosure or an investigation of serious wrongdoing
      `it would restrain corrective or reasonable management action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you want stopped or remedied is appropriate corrective action under s 66 or reasonable management action
      `I applied about the same matter under another integrity Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied about the same matter under ICAC Act s 79L, Ombudsman Act s 31U or LECC Act s 97K
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I apply for an injunction` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `I applied about the same matter under another integrity Act` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 37(11) "not entitled"
           IF `it would restrain corrective or reasonable management action` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 37(6) "may not be granted"
           IF (NOT `the conduct is or would be a detrimental action offence`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (outside the grant's own words; fork F5)
           IF `it is a public interest disclosure` `the kind of my disclosure` OR `detrimental action has been or may be taken against me` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (not one of the applicants s 37(1) names; fork F5)

-- s 37(2), (4): the terms may restrain, require a remedy, require a formal apology, restrain an attempt to end
-- employment, or require reinstatement; s 37(5) reinstatement is to be complied with despite any other law.
@export Can a detrimental action injunction order this (s 37(2), (4), (6))?
GIVEN `the order I want` IS A `The order I want` @desc The order you want. One of: "an order restraining conduct that would be a detrimental action offence", "an order requiring an act or thing to remedy a detrimental action offence", "a formal apology", "an order restraining an attempt to end my employment in a position or role", "reinstatement in the same or a substantially similar position or role", "some other order"
      `it would restrain corrective or reasonable management action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order would restrain or remedy appropriate corrective action under s 66 or reasonable management action
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the injunction order this` MEANS
    IF `it would restrain corrective or reasonable management action`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the order I want` EQUALS `some other order`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 37(2) "may", s 37(4) "to avoid doubt": other terms are neither in nor out)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 38 -- costs`

-- s 38(1) "A person who institutes proceedings under section 35 or 37 is not liable to pay costs incurred by another party
-- ... unless (a) the person instituted the proceedings vexatiously or without reasonable cause, or (b) the person's
-- unreasonable act or omission caused the other party to incur the costs." s 38(2): the other party bears the onus.
-- Fork F6: once an "unless" limb is shown, the ordinary costs rules decide, so NOTHING.
@export Can I be ordered to pay the other side's costs in my damages or injunction proceedings (s 38)?
GIVEN `I brought the proceedings under section 35 or 37` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you started the proceedings for damages (s 35) or an injunction (s 37) under this Act
      `the other side showed I brought them vexatiously or without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other party has satisfied the court that you brought the proceedings vexatiously or without reasonable cause
      `the other side showed my unreasonable act or omission caused its costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other party has satisfied the court that your unreasonable act or omission caused it to incur the costs
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I be ordered to pay the other side's costs` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `I brought the proceedings under section 35 or 37`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 38 reaches only proceedings under ss 35 and 37)
           IF `the other side showed I brought them vexatiously or without reasonable cause` OR `the other side showed my unreasonable act or omission caused its costs` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the "unless" is met; the ordinary costs rules decide; fork F6)
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 40, 41 -- protection from liability for making the disclosure`

-- s 40(1) "the maker of a public interest disclosure, in relation to the making of the disclosure (a) does not incur civil
-- liability, including ... for breaching a duty of secrecy or confidentiality ... (b) does not incur criminal liability
-- ... (c) is not liable to disciplinary action." Note 1: absolute privilege in defamation (Defamation Act 2005). s 40(2):
-- for a witness disclosure "only to the extent that the information disclosed (a) is relevant to the investigation, or
-- (b) constitutes an independent disclosure showing or tending to show serious wrongdoing". s 7(2)(b): no protection
-- for failing to comply with a duty to disclose under another law. s 41(1): no protection against liability for the
-- maker's own past conduct disclosed.
@export Am I protected from this liability for making my public interest disclosure (ss 7(2), 40, 41(1))?
GIVEN `the kind of my disclosure` IS A `The kind of disclosure` @desc The kind of disclosure you made (see "What kind of public interest disclosure did I make"). One of: "a voluntary public interest disclosure", "a voluntary public interest disclosure by determination of the head of an agency", "a witness public interest disclosure", "a mandatory public interest disclosure", "not a public interest disclosure"
      `the liability I am worried about` IS A `The liability I am worried about` @desc The liability you are worried about. One of: "civil liability, including for breaching a duty of secrecy or confidentiality" (including defamation), "criminal liability, including for breaching a confidentiality law or code of conduct", "disciplinary action", "liability for not complying with a duty to disclose information imposed by another law", "liability for my own past conduct that I revealed in making the disclosure"
      `the information is relevant to the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a witness disclosure only: whether the information you gave is relevant to the investigation
      `the information independently shows serious wrongdoing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a witness disclosure only: whether the information is an independent disclosure showing or tending to show serious wrongdoing
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I protected from this liability` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`it is a public interest disclosure` `the kind of my disclosure`)) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 40 speaks only of the maker of a public interest disclosure; other protection may come from other laws)
           IF `the liability I am worried about` EQUALS `liability for not complying with a duty to disclose information imposed by another law` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 7(2)(b) "does not protect"
           IF `the liability I am worried about` EQUALS `liability for my own past conduct that I revealed in making the disclosure` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 41(1) "does not protect"
           IF     `the kind of my disclosure` EQUALS `a witness public interest disclosure`
              AND (NOT `the information is relevant to the investigation`)
              AND (NOT `the information independently shows serious wrongdoing`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 40(2) "only to the extent"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 41(2)-(5): the Attorney General may give an undertaking (conditionally or not) that the disclosure of past conduct,
-- or the fact of it, will not be used in evidence against the person; if given, it "is not admissible in evidence
-- against the person in civil or criminal proceedings, other than proceedings relating to the falsity of the
-- disclosure". Without an undertaking, or in falsity proceedings, the Act does not say (NOTHING).
@export Can what I revealed about my own past conduct in my disclosure be used in evidence against me (s 41)?
GIVEN `the Attorney General gave me an undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Attorney General has given you an undertaking under s 41 that the disclosure will not be used in evidence against you
      `the undertaking's conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any conditions attached to the undertaking are met (answer yes if it was unconditional)
      `the proceedings are about the falsity of my disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proceedings in which it would be used relate to the falsity of your disclosure
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my disclosure of past conduct be used against me` MEANS
    IF `the Attorney General gave me an undertaking` AND `the undertaking's conditions are met` AND (NOT `the proceedings are about the falsity of my disclosure`)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 41(4) "is not admissible"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the Act is silent; the law of evidence and s 9 decide)
